# [INPUT]: Depends on Flutter and native desktop toolchains for generated local artifacts.
# [OUTPUT]: Keeps source-owned App platform scaffolds trackable while excluding caches and build output.
# [POS]: Serves as the App workspace's version-control boundary for generated files.
# [PROTOCOL]: Update this header when this file changes, then review AGENTS.md

# Miscellaneous
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.build/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.swiftpm/
migrate_working_dir/

# IntelliJ related
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# The .vscode folder contains launch configuration and tasks you configure in
# VS Code which you may wish to be included in version control, so this line
# is commented out by default.
#.vscode/

# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/flutter/ephemeral/
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/build/
/coverage/

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release
